  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia PNG Law &amp; Justice Partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Australia Papua New Guinea Law and Justice Partnership (APLJ) is the flagship program that will build on, and progress, positive outcomes of previous Australian investments in the law and justice sector.  APLJ will support a safer and more secure PNG through its support to PNG&#x2019;s law and justice sector to deliver more accessible and inclusive justice services. It will maintain a focus on addressing issues such as Gender-Based Violence, Sorcery-Accusation Related Violence (SARV), and corruption. It will strengthen village courts and land mediation mechanisms, as well as support wider inter-agency engagement and facilitation of policy implementation at national and subnational levels. There are several small value projects housed under this flagship investment, which all support the overarching goal and the program outcomes of APLJ.</narrative>
  </description>
